<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Phase 2 Best in Slot Gear list for Enhancement Shaman DPS in Wrath of the Lich King Classic. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from Ulduar. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, BoE World drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">Best in Slot Gear for Enhancement Shaman DPS in Phase 2</h2>Enhancement <a class="icontiny c7" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/shaman">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_shaman.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shaman</span></a> Tier 8 set has good bonuses which you will want to get as quickly as possible, although you might want to delay breaking up your Tier 7 until you have multiple high item level pieces to replace it with, as the <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=60169/flurry-haste-speedup">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Flurry Haste Speedup</span></a> 4-piece bonus is also very strong.<br/>
<br/>While <b>Spellhance</b> has been discussed before, what it really means is that you should have a <b>
<span class="c4">Spell Power weapon to use as a mid-fight swap</span> to snapshot Spell Power</b> into your <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=2894/fire-elemental-totem">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_fire_elemental_totem.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fire Elemental Totem</span></a> and when focusing on area of effect damage with <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=61657/fire-nova">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_fire_sealoffire.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fire Nova</span></a> and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=49271/chain-lightning">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_chainlightning.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Chain Lightning</span></a>, as they scale with Spell Power instead of traditional melee stats (AP does convert to SP with <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=30814/mental-quickness">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_mentalquickness.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mental Quickness</span></a>, but only at a 30% rate).<br/>
<br/>There are no more high item level slow caster main hands in Tier 8 which you could use to top damage on every situation, thus you will want a Physical main-hand for single target scenarios <b>and</b> a Spell Power main-hand to snapshot your Fire Elemental and AoE scenarios. We present below gear setup suggestions and optimizations for focusing on single target or AoE but the <b>main benefit can be obtained at any time by simply <span class="c4">swapping your weapon mid-combat</span></b>.<br/>
<br/>In Wrath, 26.23 Hit Rating converts into 1% Spell Hit at level 70. Unfortunately, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=30819/dual-wield-specialization">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_dualwieldspecialization.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dual Wield Specialization</span></a> does <b>not</b> give Spell Hit, thus the cap is 17% Spell Hit from gear alone, which can be reduced to 14% (or 13% if you are Alliance due to <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=6562/heroic-presence">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_21.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Heroic Presence</span></a>) with the help of <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=33602/improved-faerie-fire">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_faeriefire.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Improved Faerie Fire</span></a> or <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=33193/misery">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_misery.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Misery</span></a>. Thus, the exact amount of Spell Hit you want from your gear depends on the content you are optimizing for, and your faction. As a Horde player in a raid, you will need 26.23 * 14 = 	367.22 rating in order to cap Spell Hit, for example.<br/>
<br/>You will also be well over the 8% special attack melee Hit cap by then, as although 32.78 Hit Rating is required for 1%, you get 6% for free with <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=30819/dual-wield-specialization">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_dualwieldspecialization.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dual Wield Specialization</span></a>, thus only needing 32.78 * 2 = 65.56 rating. Extra Hit rating over specials cap will still increase your white hit damage and enable more <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=51532/maelstrom-weapon">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shaman_maelstromweapon.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Maelstrom Weapon</span></a> procs, which is a decent benefit.<br/>
<br/>
<b>Also, while we list the very strong <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45620/starshard-edge">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_weapon_shortblade_92.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Starshard Edge</span></a> as the chase weapon in the Area Damage setup, this can be a very difficult weapon to get because of high caster competition, thus make sure to look out for good alternatives, such as <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45612/constellus">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_mace_92.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Constellus</span></a> (and make sure to use <span class="c4">Hit gems</span> to compensate if you do).</b>
<br/>
