<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="weapons">Weapons, Shields, Off-hands and Totems for Enhancement Shaman DPS in Phase 2</h2>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="1-handed-weapons-for-enhancement-shaman-dps-in-phase-2">1-Handed Weapons for Enhancement Shaman DPS in Phase 2</h4>Due to <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=16284/flurry">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_ghoulfrenzy.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Flurry</span></a> having a 0.5 seconds cooldown on being consumed, <b>having weapons of matching speed</b> is very important in order to minimize attack desynching and maximize your Flurry uptime. Most of the main-hand (MH) and off-hand (OH) weapons we list below have similar speeds and weapons with the same speed are meant to be used <b>together</b>, whenever possible.<br/>
<br/>Also, as much of an Enhancement <a class="icontiny c7" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/shaman">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_shaman.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shaman</span></a>'s damage comes from spells that scale with Spell Power rather than Weapon DPS /<wbr/> Attack Power (other than <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=30814/mental-quickness">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_mentalquickness.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mental Quickness</span></a>), picking up a caster weapon is recommended for trash or bosses with multiple adds, and it performs decently in single target as well.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="weapons-for-enhancement-shaman-dps-in-phase-2">Weapons for Enhancement Shaman DPS in Phase 2</h4>While <a class="q5 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=46017/valanyr-hammer-of-ancient-kings">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_mace_99.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Val'anyr, Hammer of Ancient Kings</span></a> is, technically, the best Spell Power weapon in Ulduar, it should be reserved for Healer specs first and foremost. Make sure to use it for Enhancement if you happen to have obtained it due to your Restoration off-spec, however!<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45132/golden-saronite-dragon">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_weapon_hand_23.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Golden Saronite Dragon</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45620/starshard-edge">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_weapon_shortblade_92.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Starshard Edge</span></a> (<b>heavily contested</b>) are the two best Phase 2 main-hand weapons, with Golden Saronite Dragon being a physical-focused main hand option and Starshard Edge being a strong Spell Power option.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45612/constellus">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_mace_92.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Constellus</span></a>, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=46035/aesuga-hand-of-the-ardent-champion">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_mace_92.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Aesuga, Hand of the Ardent Champion</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45449/the-masticator">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_weapon_hand_22.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">The Masticator</span></a> are also great main-hand weapons and much less contested than the top choices.<br/>
<br/>Finally, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=39763/wraith-strike">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_weapon_hand_09.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Wraith Strike</span></a> <b>is still quite good</b> as the only Spell Power weapon with slow speed in the list, although it sports relatively low stats compared to Ulduar gear. Pair it with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45463/vulmir-the-northern-tempest">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_mace_91.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vulmir, the Northern Tempest</span></a> for a budget, yet powerful, setup.<br/>
<br/>
